    <item>
      <title>Trump, Xi, Putin's Trilateral Evokes Images of Yalta and Beyond</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-11-19/trump-trilateral-evokes-images-of-yalta-beyond-video</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">f581296fd40cea4a1eb63fd5</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:15:01 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>The trilateral meeting between Donald Trump, Xi Jinping and Vladimir Putin was billed as an opportunity for global cooperation — while raising fears that the leaders of the three largest nuclear powers are carving up spheres of influence.
Even if the summit was light on concrete outcomes, the images of the leaders of the US, China and Russia at an unprecedented summit is likely to live on in history.
Elizabeth Economy, Stanford Professor and Hargrove Senior Fellow, discusses the trilateral meeting and its outcomes. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
